SWEET BATTERY EXTERNAL = CHGIN_OK (patch 0397, oriole upstream port Step 8; applies after 0395): SweetBattery showed external=0 charging=0 while the phone was on USB (doc 56 Step 7 open item), because 0395 took External/Charging from FG Current > +50 mA only and a USB 2 port at 500 mA leaves the phone in net discharge; iOS therefore showed no charging state and never played the connect sound (the "chime" the user heard with the static fallback). The thermal thread's 30 s read set (sweet_chg_fg_batt) now also reads the charger 0x69 reg 0xB4 CHG_INT_OK, one byte (already on the i2c_rd_slave_ok allowlist: 0x69 n == 1, 0xB0..0xCC; the decode CHGIN_OK = bit 6 is upstream 0284 phase 2), with the same guards and the same failure rule as the FG reads (a failed read stops the bus). sweet_batt_ext() hands the last CHGIN_OK to SweetBattery: External/Capable/Charging = CHGIN_OK || Current > +50 mA; one log line `SWEET BATTERY: external N (CHGIN_OK N, FG current N mA) (patch 0397)` on every change. READS ONLY: no write, no new register outside the allowlist, no boot-arg.

